 in the deepwater producing Baobab field in Block CI-40, offshore Cote d'Ivoire in West Africa. Further, the company owns production and working interests in Cardium light oil and Mannville liquids-rich gas assets in Harmattan, within the Western Canadian Sedimentary Basin, approximately 80 kilometers north of Calgary, Alberta; and a 60% working interest in an undeveloped portion of block P offshore Equatorial Guinea. VAALCO Energy, Inc. was incorporated in 1985 and is headquartered in Houston, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. George Walter-Mitchell Maxwell | CEO & Director | Age 59 | Compensation: $1.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 281 people. Revenue per employee of $1.3M ranks in the below the sector median among Energy peers. Stock-based compensation of $22K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["VAALCO Energy, Inc. is a small-cap energy business with a $578M market cap on $359M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +0% over the past three years and +16% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 20% against a 9% cost of capital \u2014 a 11-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and thin -3.1\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 4.7% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 3.2% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 2/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Operating margins 21% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 7.5% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Payout ratio of 93% leaves thin coverage if earnings wobble","sev":"amber","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Energy peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"The commodity cycle \u2014 revenue and free cash flow are ultimately hostage to a price the company does not set, and the long-run energy-transition arc adds a structural overhang.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Geopolitical supply shocks \u2014 wars, sanctions, and OPEC decisions create volatility that no hedging programme can fully neutralise.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Energy sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter","Energy ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"(EGY) Risk Channels and Responsive Allocation","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/24/EGY_Risk_Channels_and_Responsive_Allocation_110726090201_1794060121.html","date":"2026-11-07","timestamp":1794060121.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.202,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"VAALCO Energy Inc (EGY) (Q3 2026) Earnings Call Highlights: Record Adjusted EBITDAX of $71. ...","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/energy/articles/vaalco-energy-inc-egy-q3-211632191.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793999792.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.796,"tier":0